  "summary": "CGI versions from 4.71 before 5.00 for Perl allow denial of service via a plain string dereferenced as a symbolic…",
  "details": "CGI versions from 4.71 before 5.00 for Perl allow denial of service via a plain string dereferenced as a symbolic reference in uploadInfo.\n\nuploadInfo dereferences its argument and calls its filename method without checking that it is an upload filehandle. A plain string naming a defined global variable, such as the parameter value from ?upload=0, is treated as a symbolic reference, and the method call on it dies.",
  "severity": [
    {
